Project: demo-cpm (Firestore Emulator at 127.0.0.1:8080)
This is emulator-only evidence; it is not production Firestore or Vercel proof.

Emulator command:
$ npx -y firebase-tools@13 emulators:start --only firestore --project demo-cpm --config /home/ubuntu/harness/firebase-r02.json
Observed ready endpoint: Firestore 127.0.0.1:8080.

Harnesses:
- Fixed branch: http://127.0.0.1:4175 (project root /home/ubuntu/repos/cpmwall3)
- Baseline: http://127.0.0.1:4176 (separate worktree at c67f23b)
- Both use FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST=127.0.0.1:8080 and the dummy JWT secret
  test-secret-long-random-value-for-route-proof.
- Each harness received FIREBASE_SERVICE_KEY as throwaway demo-cpm service-account
  JSON with a freshly generated RSA private key. No real credentials were used.
- Seed/helper script: evidence/r02_seed.mjs; it generates a fresh throwaway RSA key.

Seeded documents: users/ADMINU (role ADMIN), users/BOB (ip 203.0.113.7),
users/CAROL (no ip), posts/test-post, settings/filters, and pinned/current.
No fingerprint_bans documents are seeded. Every post request includes both
x-forwarded-for and x-vercel-forwarded-for because post.js trusts the latter,
not the arbitrary x-forwarded-for header alone.

The same-IP rate_limits document is explicitly deleted before the CAROL test.
Per-request curl commands, response headers, status lines, and bodies follow.

